      "evidence": "The hypersurface supplier [F5] constructs a “locally flat” three-manifold R using topological microbundle transversality. The scoped item’s [F6] says smooth-chain results are used “only in smooth ambient neighborhoods, not by treating a locally flat R as an already smooth submanifold.” Proof 3.1 nevertheless says chains “in R can be taken smooth” by applying [F6]. The supplier does not give R a smooth embedded structure, so [F6] does not license this step. The later general argument in Proof 4.2 uses continuous chains and disjoint smooth ambient neighborhoods, so the item’s overall conclusion has an alternate route; this smooth-only subproof gap is nonfatal.",
